      "text": "Biomechanics applies continuum mechanics — the same stress/strain tensor formalism you know\nfrom structural engineering — to biological materials. The difference: biological materials are\nnonlinear, anisotropic, viscoelastic, heterogeneous, and alive (they remodel in response to load)."
    }
